  <p class="headerText">About Me</p>

  As a advocate for the sharing of knowledge, I'm the Director of <a href="https://foss.wiki" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FOSS Wiki</a>, A comprehensive wiki for Free
  and Open Source Software and Linux related topics! Not biased or anything, but you should check it out and help contribute, any edit or improvement is welcome! I also run a
  tracker for MP's stances on <a href="https://transmps.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trans Rights</a>.

  <br /><br />
  I occasionally program too, i'm not super proficient but I know a bit of Golang, Python and JavaScript (and guess what, HTML and CSS too!). You can find my projects and contributions
  on <a href="https://github.com/atmois" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.

  <br /><br />
  Some of my non-techy interests include science, space, music and law (yes I'm boring) alongside a million other random obsessions. My music taste is one of the most random things out
  there. You can see what I'm listening to on <a href="https://listenbrainz.org/user/atmois" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ListenBrainz</a>. My current obssession you
  might ask? <b>MCR</b>, favourite songs being <b>Party Poison and DEAD!</b>

  <br /><br />

  I love reading, although I don't do it as much as I should. Some of my favourite books are the "His Dark Materials" series, Randall Munroe's books, A Series of Unfortunate
  Events, the Divergent series and the original Hunger Games trilogy. The last book I read (this will be out of date rather often) was
  <b> The "One of Us Is Lying" series by Karen M. McManus.</b>

  <br /><br />
  In typical nerd fashion I also love video games. Some of my favourite games are
  <b> the Portal series, Minecraft, Satisfactory, The Finals, Team Fortress 2, Celeste, Cities Skylines, Subnautica, Cyberpunk 2077 and really any open world game.</b>
  If you want to see what games I'm currently playing you can check out my <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/id/atmois" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam</a> profile.

  <br /><br />
  I run a custom Bazzite image on my PC and Laptop which you can see <a href="https://github.com/atmois/atmo-bazzite" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>! On my
